# Opinion

Meeting: 0009-fix-player-not-loading-into-match-in-rpsarena
Agent: Developer
Task: Fix player not loading into match in RPSArena
Context:
  - The client only showed a queued toast and never re-polled `/api/matchmaking`, so the first player never saw the match payload after pairing.
  - There was no shared, testable helper to manage matchmaking polling or guard against overlapping fetches.
  - Coverage target remains 100% across Node tests and repo-level pytest.
Position:
  - Introduce a reusable matchmaking poller that repeatedly calls the endpoint until a matched payload arrives or an error occurs.
  - Wire the UI to start polling automatically after a queued response so the player receives the match id/opponent without manual retries.
Recommendations:
  - Add a dedicated `MatchmakingPoller` module with scheduler injection and re-entry protection, plus thorough tests for queued, matched, error, and misconfigured flows.
  - Update `public/main.js` to reuse the poller on queue/bot flows, surface matched status with opponent context, and cancel polling on completion or failure.
  - Keep `npm test` (c8 --100) and repo `pytest --maxfail=1` in the workflow to ensure coverage stays perfect.
